  message: "[REVIEW 2026-11-15: REAL TODAY, TEXT PARTLY STALE] 2026-11-15, dev e2b6ab8096, fixture run. js_module/.ts limb: not occurring (main.ts, widget.ts, util.js carry one file node each; no node has origin js-module-linker; fix 4549106aec). WI-babuk limb: not occurring (one `javascript:src/util.js` node). SFC limb: live when components use each other: in that fixture 4 of 4 .svelte/.vue paths carry two file nodes; in a second fixture of two SFC files with no component use each carried one (`javascript:` + `svelte:`/`vue:`), including `vue:src/Child.svelte:1-1:file:file` from vue-component-linker. The statement's 5 htrac-frontend paths no longer exist (removed 86cb7d3a37). cli.py:7244-7247 is now cli.py:13159-13169. Self-analysis: one path with 3 kind=file nodes, toml script entries on packages/hypergumbo-tracker/pyproject.toml (WI-dofif, wont_do). Full review: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/stable_id_items_review_11152026/reports/INV-movor.md. No status or priority change made by this review."  # cbe5
- op: discuss  # d191
  at: '2026-11-15T19:47:30Z'  # d191
  by: agent  # d191
  actor: jgstern_agent  # d191
  clock: 10  # d191
  nonce: d191  # d191
  message: "[INVESTIGATION 2026-11-15, owner-requested: this item against the ADRs, the spec and the project's intent; dev e2b6ab8096] (1) The statement as written cannot stand. ADR-0036 Ruling 3, as amended by WI-dipim, lets kind=file also carry manifest entries with meta entry_role (npm script or main, pyproject script; audit-findings 0005), and WI-dofif-nidon-fuhip-migib-ribob-bilov-ruzur-hotif was retracted for that reason. \"Exactly one file-kind Symbol per path\" is therefore false by design. The property the documents rely on is narrower: one FILE PSEUDO-SYMBOL per path (name file, kind file, span 1-1, make_file_id). Spec line 1436 defines metrics.debug.analyzed_file_symbols as the count of kind=file nodes and reads it as a file count. (2) The narrower property is violated today on .svelte/.vue paths whose components use each other: two pseudo-symbols per path, javascript: (the JavaScript analyzer, for the script block) beside svelte:/vue: (orchestrator synthesis for the component analyzer, or vue-component-linker, which hard-codes vue and so labels a .svelte file vue). On the fixture analyzed_file_symbols is 12 for 8 paths. Two components that do not use each other got one node each. (3) Measured consequence: the file's edges are split. Script imports and the call to helper() start at javascript:src/App.svelte; the component import starts at svelte:src/App.svelte; main.ts's import lands on the javascript: node; the component link lands on vue:src/Child.svelte. A consumer walking from either node sees part of the file. (4) What the single node should be, per the ADRs: ADR-0031 defines Symbol.language as the source language of the declaration, and the declaration here is the FILE, which is a Svelte or Vue file; INV-ronuf-hazag-mumut-rozih-rumig-sugif-dijip-sijiz (satisfied) already says a synthesized file Symbol takes its language from the file extension. Symbols inside <script> are JavaScript and stay so. ADR-0057 is the doctrine for two producers of one declaration: one record with both passes in origin, not two records. (5) Nothing enforces it: spec_validator has no one-pseudo-symbol-per-path check, and the four instances so far (websocket INV-ronuf-hazag-mumut-rozih-rumig-sugif-dijip-sijiz; js_module, this item 05-19; importer-language WI-babuk-nufoh-rolig-sabus-gobuk-zituh-sofup-holid; components, 11-01) were each found by hand. RECOMMENDATION, owner's call, nothing changed: keep this invariant as the carrier instead of closing it into WI-modan-tizob-bilag-fanas-simip-guzuz-homoj-rimut, which is a P3 work item about phantom import targets whose point 5 only mentions this. Rewrite the header: title \"every path has exactly one file pseudo-symbol across producers (live: .svelte/.vue paths carry javascript: beside svelte:/vue:)\"; statement narrowed to the pseudo-symbol and naming the manifest-entry exclusion; root_cause \"each producer picks the language slot itself (its own language, the importer's, or a hard-coded vue) and no check compares\"; close condition \"a validator check for one file pseudo-symbol per path, at 0 on a fleet measurement\". Fixtures: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/stable_id_items_review_11152026/work/INV-movor and work/v_movor."  # d191
